        "id": 18786,
        "name": "Anubis",
        "username": "Anubis",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/anubis/{size}/4949_2.png",
        "created_at": "2018-12-06T11:03:22.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>Hey I really enjoy the simplicity of this system it's a fabulous system but I got a bunch of questions (I'm hyper when I'm excited)&nbsp;</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>1: I talked to Chris at Origins and he said Prime Wardens will be a supplement. As vaguely as you wanna get how much info is in a supplement like Prime Wardens? Five heroes, a supervillain they've fought and maybe an environment?&nbsp;</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>2: Using Character Creation rules can I be a Tokusatsu hero? I mean more Kamen Rider where my 'forms' are the entire character, not a hero who has forms and fights but say a hero who has several forms and most of their abilities are from transforming. Unlike Meurto and Bunker who can change forms but can do stuff besides that my character concept can't <em>fight </em>without transforming. I was thinking maybe like 2 abilities per zone that my hero always has access to and then like 3 different forms and say 3 on two of them and 2 on third and I don't need to be in a particular GYRO to use any. Can I have that? More flashy transformations over utility?&nbsp;</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>3: Can we expect to see Holiday themed one shots? A Halloween one fighting like a Scarecrow parody be pretty awesome.</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>",
        "post_number": 1,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T01:52:15.937Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
        "reply_to_post_number": null,
